config CM
    bool "Command mode support"
    default y

config CM_BUF_SIZE_KiB
    int "Command buffer size in KiB"
    default 4096
    depends on CM

config CM_TRANSPORT_READY_TIMEOUT
    int "Timeout in seconds before transport must become ready"
    default 10
    range 1 4294
    depends on CM
    help
        How long command mode waits for a host while it has no session.
        Then pb resets (command-mode.md 2.2). pb's timeouts count
        microseconds in 32 bits, hence at most 4294 s. A value outside the
        range isn't used: the build takes the default.

config CM_TRANSFER_TIMEOUT
    int "Timeout in seconds for a transfer inside a command"
    default 10
    range 1 65
    depends on CM
    help
        How long command mode waits for the host to complete a transfer
        inside a command, kicking the watchdog meanwhile. Then the session
        ends and the transport is restarted (command-mode.md 4.6). The caps
        carry it in milliseconds, in 16 bits, hence at most 65 s.

config CM_AUTH
    bool "Enable command mode authentication"
    default y
    depends on CM
    help
        Command mode's gate (command-mode.md 3.2). On: a closed device (a
        locked or an unknown life cycle) answers only DEVICE_IDENTIFIER_READ
        and AUTHENTICATE until the session authenticates, and the build
        selects at least one method below, or it doesn't build.

        Off: no gate. Every session counts as authenticated, so command
        mode is open in every life cycle state, also on a locked device.
        That is the product's choice, made in its defconfig (D-059).

config CM_AUTH_TOKEN
    bool "Token based authentication"
    depends on CM_AUTH
    help
        Authenticate using the signature of the hash, of the device UUID

config CM_AUTH_PASSWORD
    bool "Password based authentication"
    depends on CM_AUTH
    help
        Authenticate using a password. This requires a board level implementation.

config SLC_EOL
    bool "End of life (EOL) as a life cycle state the device can enter"
    default n
    depends on CM
    help
        The product's choice (system.md 4). On: SLC_SET_EOL moves the device
        to the SoC's end of life state through the port's set_eol, where the
        port has one. It can't be undone, and command mode is open again in
        that state (D-011).

        Off, the default: the device can't enter EOL. SLC_SET_EOL answers
        NOT_SUPPORTED and slc_set_eol() calls nothing of the port's
        (command-mode.md 4.5, 5.2). A device that is in EOL already still
        reads as that.
